                  ],
                  "tip": "Identify the relevant conservation or field equation, then test the prediction in the lab."
                },
                {
                  "summary": [
                    "<p>A local field may be nonzero even when a small loop has zero circulation.</p>",
                    "<p>Zero curl forces the electric field itself to vanish.</p>"
                  ],
                  "tip": "Identify the relevant conservation or field equation, then test the prediction in the lab."
                },
                {
                  "summary": [
                    "<p>Steady charge implies zero net outward charge flux from a fixed volume.</p>",
                    "<p>Larger current density always implies net outward current.</p>"
                  ],
                  "tip": "Identify the relevant conservation or field equation, then test the prediction in the lab."
                },
                {
                  "summary": [
                    "<p>Electromagnetic energy flux is E × H and depends on the chosen outward normal.</p>",
